<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Montereau-Fault-Yonne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Montereau-Fault-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonne-river">Yonne</a> is a town in the Seine-et-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, where the Yonne flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a>. On 10 September 1419 Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-the-fearless">John the Fearless of Burgundy</a> was killed there on the bridge during a meeting with the Dauphin Charles, driving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> into alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. In 1814 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> won a battle against the Austrians and Württembergers at the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/montereau-fault-yonne.jpg" alt="Montereau-Fault-Yonne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjism89 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montereau-Fault-Yonne_-_City_center_seen_from_North_bank_-_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
